From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:40:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve attribute aliases with a fetch default instead of a
 block

`resolve_attribute_name` looks up aliases with
`attribute_aliases.fetch(super, &:itself)`. For every name without an
alias, the common case, `fetch` calls its block, and `&:itself` turns
that into a `Symbol#to_proc` call. Passing the resolved name as the
default returns it without the block. `attribute_aliases` is still
read before `super` converts the name, and `fetch` still ignores the
Hash default and returns stored `nil` values, as before.
---
 activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb b/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb
index 5d36ad5f8d..00aef7c6cc 100644
--- a/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb
+++ b/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb
@@ -423,7 +423,7 @@ def inherited(base) # :nodoc:
         end
 
         def resolve_attribute_name(name)
-          attribute_aliases.fetch(super, &:itself)
+          attribute_aliases.fetch(name = super, name)
         end
 
         def generated_attribute_methods
